{{define "main"}}
    {{- /* RG-3: closing takes the register away from every tab the household has
           open, so it is asked about rather than done on one keystroke. It
           destroys nothing, which is why the page says so plainly rather than
           warning about something that cannot happen. */ -}}
    <div class="register-head">
        <h1>Close this checkbook?</h1>
    </div>

    <dl class="problem-facts">
        <dt>Database</dt>
        <dd><code>{{.Closing}}</code></dd>
    </dl>

    <p>
        Closing does not change or delete anything. The program keeps running and lets go of the
        file, so it becomes a single file you can copy, move, or replace with a backup. You can
        open it again, or open another, without restarting.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
        Any other window you have open on this checkbook will say the same thing the next time you
        use it.
    </p>

    <form method="post" action="/checkbook/close">
        {{- /* The generation of the checkbook this page was drawn for. A tab
               that has been on screen since before a swap is refused rather than
               closing a database it was never looking at (CO-3). */ -}}
        <input type="hidden" name="generation" value="{{.Generation}}">
        <div class="entry-fields">
            <div class="f-add"><button type="submit">Close checkbook</button></div>
            <div class="f-add"><a class="cta" href="/">Keep it open</a></div>
        </div>
    </form>
{{end}}
